# Craft

Apply this before editing the app. Domain facts stay in `project.mdc`.

## Clean

- Put code in the feature module that already owns it: `auth_routes`, `dashboard`, `profile`, `debts`, `expenses`, `spends`, `admin_users`, `db_admin`, `formatting`, `web`.
- Reuse `format_toman`, `persian_digits`, `render`, and `flash`. Do not add a second formatter or a new CSS framework.
- Change only what the task needs. Do not leave unused files, routes, or helpers.
- New priced holdings still follow the asset checklist in `project.mdc`.

```text
# ❌ BAD — a new assets list inside a template
# ✅ GOOD — loop ASSET_ORDER, same as the dashboard
```

## Security

- Every state-changing form uses `require_csrf` and a hidden `csrf` field.
- Rows belong to the logged-in user (`user_id`). Admin pages check `is_admin`.
- Do not log, render, or commit passwords, `SECRET_KEY`, Sanjeh tokens, or MCP tokens.
- Show a short Persian error. Do not send exception text or a stack trace to the page.
- Do not add a route that skips the session check.

```text
# ❌ BAD — db.query(Debt).all()
# ✅ GOOD — filter Debt.user_id == user.id
```

## UI

- Persian, RTL, existing classes: `card`, `btn`, `tabs`, `grid-form`, `data-table`, `toast`.
- Money is Toman, formatted with `format_toman`. Quantities use `format_qty`.
- Keep the current type (Vazirmatn) and colors. A new screen should look like the dashboard and profile, not a new product.

## Mobile

The stylesheet already breaks at 900px, 720px, and 520px. A layout change must still work at 520px wide.

- Stack forms and toolbars; do not force a wide horizontal layout.
- Put wide tables in `table-wrap` so the page itself does not scroll sideways.
- Number fields stay `dir="ltr"` with `inputmode`. Buttons stay full width when the existing mobile rules do that.
- Do not shrink tap targets below the current `.btn` size.

```text
# ❌ BAD — a new table with no table-wrap and a fixed 800px width
# ✅ GOOD — table-wrap plus a 520px check of the same screen
```
